Kieran Connell's BBC Master 128 emulator core ("kc-beeb"): a cycle-stepped 65C12 and Master 128
written from scratch for small microcontrollers, checked frame by frame against beebjit.
  https://github.com/kieranhj/esp32-beeb  (its main/ directory)
  commit ca72230 ("PLAN: BOOT in the menu tried on the board")
Licence: GNU GPL v3 (LICENSE at the top). teletext_glyphs.h: B-em's character set (Sarah Walker
and others, GPL).

Only the machine is copied (the files here, from main/); the ESP32 platform, host tools, ROMs and
discs are not. Its RP2350 glue lives in src/machines/master.

Since then, merged from upstream (its later commits, written for Evil Influences):
  dcf074b..2d265dd (to "Paging reads through the quiet window", 2026-10-14) in crtc.c, crtc.h,
  machine.c, machine.h and render.c: the CRTC's vsync bound counts line ends to R7 (no machine
  sync at every line end of a short line), crtc_short_lines and crtc_short_block for R0 < 8 lines,
  CRTC register and paging accesses through the quiet window, display writes catching up the
  CRTC alone, the display write window counted in rows, the renderer's run loops taking DISPEN
  changes and row address events, and a renderer hang fix at the right edge. With two changes so
  that struct machine keeps its layout (saved states made of it stay valid):
  - machine.h: win_extent is a uint16_t in what was padding after irq_late (upstream: a
    uint32_t added before win_due); machine.c clamps it to 0x4000 (all of RAM anyway).
  - crtc.h, crtc.c: the short-line statistics (stat_short and friends) are static counters in
    crtc.c under MACHINE_STATS, not fields of struct crtc.

Local changes, each kept small:

- cpu6502.c, cpu6502.h: the CPU's registers and flags kept as 32-bit fields (byte-sized fields
  cost the M33 a bit-field insert at every write; about 10 points of core 0 at real speed).
- machine.c: two counts of the VIAs' 1 MHz ticks no longer shift the absolute cycle count, which
  went wrong when the 32-bit count wrapped (a hang after 35.8 minutes).
- render.c, render.h: two pixel tables of each kind kept (Elite's MODE 4 top and MODE 5 dashboard
  rebuilt a 4 KB table twice a frame).
- machine.c, machine.h: machine_set_analogue(): the ADC's channels carry values (an analogue
  joystick), kept outside struct machine so its layout stays as it was.
- disc.c, disc.h, fdc.c: saved games: the tracks the 1770 writes are counted and marked dirty,
  disc_read_sector() reads a sector back out of the pulses; disc_load_ssd() reports progress.

Each was checked to give identical pictures on the test discs (docs/master/README.md).
src/common/machine_hook.h (the interface for a program built in alongside the machine) is not
part of this core.
